course: dictionary
lesson: 15291
title: Formal words for places
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Situated means placed or found in a certain place. You will often see it in maps, reports and formal descriptions, where writers need to say exactly where something is. «The school is situated near the river.» The clue is near the river, so situated tells you where the school is found.
explain: Read the words around it to check. In «The shop is well situated, close to the bus stop and the car park», the words close to the bus stop show that well situated means in a good position for people to reach it.
explain: In everyday talk, people usually say is or is near instead. «The school is near the river» means the same as «The school is situated near the river», but it sounds less formal. Swap the simpler words in and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Situated means placed or found in a certain place.
fact: «Situated» is a formal word, so you will see it in maps, reports and descriptions.
fact: «The town is situated on a hill» means the town is on a hill.
fact: «Well situated» means in a good position for something, and «badly situated» means in a poor position.
fact: Useful phrases: situated in, situated on, situated near, conveniently situated.
exercise: «The library is situated next to the park.» Where is the library? | Inside a bus | *Next to the park | Under the sea | On the moon
exercise: Which everyday words mean the same as «is situated» in simple speech? | Is very tall | Is shouting | Is eaten | *Is near
exercise: A report says «The hotel is conveniently situated for the station.» What does conveniently situated suggest? | Moving from place to place | *In a good place, easy to reach | Lost and hard to find | In a dark, quiet place
test: Which word is formal and means placed or found in a certain place? | Curious | *Situated | Hungry | Sleepy
test: Which phrase means in a good position for something? | Very loud | Badly hidden | Slowly moving | *Well situated
exam: Which sentence uses situated correctly? | The cat situated happily on the mat. | Situated is a lovely brown dog. | *The school is situated near the river. | The sky situated loudly over the hill.
